      "writtenOn": "2025-09-23T23:30:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the issue is one of timing. Or possibly there is always an event at init time to check the value of GPIO_TABLET_MODE_L as there may not be an edge to trigger an interrupt if it\u0027s already at 0 when the EC reboots. \n\nThe interrupt handler calls lid_angle_peripheral_enable(0) and this in turn appears to trigger something that is clearing the refresh bit in boot_keys_value. The interrupt is subsequently disabled, but by this time it\u0027s already too late as the refresh bit has already been cleared.",
      "parentUuid": "e026a483_f72e07b8",
      "revId": "44c5ea75e3db8e552b807b8911738ff7d99b103a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b6e492e_e1133c77",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1262393
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-24T01:59:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right, this is timing issue. \nIn motionsense_init() to check clamshell mode to do gmr_tablet_switch_disable(), this priority is used HOOK_PRIO_DEFAULT. \n\nBut disable keyboard scan is in gmr_tablet_switch_init of lid_angle_peripheral_enable(0) which used HOOK_PRIO_POST_LID, this timing is early motionsense_init(). Cause KB scan disable cannot scan refresh key.\nI think we can change the gmr_tablet_switch_init priority to later than motionsense_init(). Please let me know for more advise.",
      "parentUuid": "3c235c96_4c323c97",
      "revId": "44c5ea75e3db8e552b807b8911738ff7d99b103a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
